 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity**: $O(N \cdot S)$, where $N$ is the number of reflection bounces and $S$ is the number of SDF evaluations per ray. Each bounce requires a full ray march.
-*   **Memory Complexity**: $O(1)$ auxiliary memory per pixel, as the recursion is typically iterative.
-*   **Performance**: Reflections significantly increase rendering cost due to multiple SDF evaluations per pixel. Performance scales linearly with the number of reflections.
-*   **Strengths**: Produces accurate specular highlights and mirror-like surfaces. Simple to implement on top of basic sphere tracing.
-*   **Limitations**: Does not account for diffuse inter-reflection (global illumination) without further extensions (e.g., path tracing). High reflection counts can cause aliasing and performance bottlenecks.
-*   **When to use**: For mirror-like surfaces, glossy materials, or when specular highlights are required.
-*   **When not to use**: For diffuse-only materials, or when performance is critical and reflections are not visually necessary.
